d(9)));","-        assert!(!inside.ends_with(ERR_OOB), \"{} lib rejected good(9)\", lib.name);","-    }"," }"," "," /// ERRORS row 11 — `good(INT_MAX)`."," #[test]"," fn err_11_good_int_max() {","-    assert_same_forked(&Op::Good(i32::MAX));","-    let mut expected = ten_lines(Some(7));","-    expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_OOB);","+    let op = Op::Good(i32::MAX);","+    assert_same(&op);","     for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","-        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Good(i32::MAX)));","-        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);","+        assert_eq!(output(lib, &op), good_rejected(), \"{} lib\", lib.name);","     }"," }"," "]},{"oldStart":153,"oldLines":105,"newStart":168,"newLines":114,"lines":[" #[test]"," fn err_12_good_out_of_range_random() {","     let mut rng = Rng::new(0xE770_0012);","-    let mut expected = ten_lines(Some(7));","-    expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_OOB);","-    for i in 0..200 {","-        let d = if i % 2 == 0 {","-            rng.range_i32(i32::MIN, -1)","-        } else {","-            rng.range_i32(10, i32::MAX)","-        };","-        assert_same(&Op::Good(d));","-        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(rust_lib(), &Op::Good(d)));","-        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"good({d})\");","+    let ops: Vec<Op> = (0..200)","+        .map(|i| {","+            Op::Good(if i % 2 == 0 {","+                rng.range_i32(i32::MIN, -1)","+            } else {","+                rng.range_i32(10, i32::MAX)","+            })","+        })","+        .collect();","+    assert_same_batch(&ops);","+    let expected = good_rejected();","+    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","+        for (out, op) in outputs(lib, &ops).iter().zip(&ops) {","+            assert_eq!(out, &expected, \"{} lib {}\", lib.name, op.describe());","+        }","     }"," }"," "," /// ERRORS row 13 — `good(9)` is the last accepted value."," #[test]"," fn err_13_good_nine_accepted() {","-    assert_same_forked(&Op::Good(9));","-    let mut expected = ten_lines(Some(7));","+    let op = Op::Good(9);","+    assert_same(&op);","+    let mut expected = g2b_block();","     expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(9)));","     for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","-        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Good(9)));","-        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);","+        assert_eq!(output(lib, &op), expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);","     }"," }"," "," /// ERRORS row 14 — `good(0)` is the lower boundary and is accepted."," #[test]"," fn err_14_good_zero_accepted() {","-    assert_same_forked(&Op::Good(0));","-    let mut expected = ten_lines(Some(7));","+    let op = Op::Good(0);","+    assert_same(&op);","+    let mut expected = g2b_block();","     expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(0)));","     for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","-        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Good(0)));","-        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);","+        assert_eq!(output(lib, &op), expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);","     }"," }"," "," /// ERRORS row 15 — `bad(0)` / `bad(9)`: the boundaries the missing upper-bound","-/// check would have used are accepted and in bounds.","+/// check would have used are accepted and stay in bounds."," #[test]"," fn err_15_bad_boundaries_accepted() {","-    for (d, idx) in [(0i32, 0usize), (9, 9)] {","-        assert_same_forked(&Op::Bad(d));","-        for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","-            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Bad(d)));","-            assert_eq!(out, ten_lines(Some(idx)), \"{} lib bad({d})\", lib.name);","-        }","+    let ops = [Op::Bad(0), Op::Bad(9)];","+    assert_same_batch(&ops);","+    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","+        let out = outputs(lib, &ops);","+        assert_eq!(out[0], ten_lines(Some(0)), \"{} lib bad(0)\", lib.name);","+        assert_eq!(out[1], ten_lines(Some(9)), \"{} lib bad(9)\", lib.name);","     }"," }"," ","-/// ERRORS row 16 — `goodG2B`'s \"negative\" branch is unreachable (`data` == 7), so","-/// neither library may ever print that message from `good`/`driver`.","+/// ERRORS row 16 — `goodG2B`'s \"negative\" branch is unreachable (`data` is the","+/// literal `7`), so neither library may ever print that message from","+/// `good`/`driver`, and the fixed block always comes first."," #[test]"," fn err_16_goodg2b_error_branch_unreachable() {","     let mut rng = Rng::new(0xE770_0016);","-    let mut values = vec![-1, 0, 7, 9, 10, i32::MIN, i32::MAX];","+    let mut ops: Vec<Op> = [-1, 0, 7, 9, 10, i32::MIN, i32::MAX]","+        .iter()","+        .map(|&d| Op::Good(d))","+        .collect();","     for _ in 0..100 {","-        values.push(rng.next_i32());","+        ops.push(Op::Good(rng.next_i32()));","     }","-    for d in values {","-        for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","-            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Good(d)));","+    assert_same_batch(&ops);","+    let block = g2b_block();","+    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","+        for (out, op) in outputs(lib, &ops).iter().zip(&ops) {","             assert!(","-                !contains(&out, ERR_NEGATIVE),","-                \"{} lib printed the goodG2B 'negative' message for good({d})\",","-                lib.name","+                !contains(out, ERR_NEGATIVE),","+                \"{} lib printed goodG2B's 'negative' message for {}\",","+                lib.name,","+                op.describe()","             );","-            // the goodG2B block (index 7 set) always comes first","             assert!(","-                out.starts_with(&ten_lines(Some(7))),","-                \"{} lib: good({d}) did not start with goodG2B's fixed block\",","-                lib.name","+                out.starts_with(&block),","+                \"{} lib: {} did not start with goodG2B's fixed block\",","+                lib.name,","+                op.describe()","             );","         }","-        assert_same(&Op::Good(d));","     }"," }"," ","-fn contains(hay: &[u8], needle: &[u8]) -> bool {","-    hay.windows(needle.len()).any(|w| w == needle)","+/// The full seven-part `driver` transcript for the given inner blocks.","+fn driver_transcript(good_block: &[u8], bad_block: &[u8]) -> Vec<u8> {","+    let mut v = Vec::new();","+    v.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling good()...\\n\");","+    v.extend_from_slice(good_block);","+    v.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished good()\\n\");","+    v.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling bad()...\\n\");","+    v.extend_from_slice(bad_block);","+    v.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished bad()\\n\");","+    v"," }"," "," /// ERRORS row 17 — `driver` with both error branches taken at once."," #[test]"," fn err_17_driver_both_error_branches() {","     let op = Op::Driver(-5, -9);","-    assert_same_forked(&op);","-    let mut expected = Vec::new();","-    expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling good()...\\n\");","-    expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(7)));","-    expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_OOB);","-    expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished good()\\n\");","-    expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling bad()...\\n\");","-    expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_NEGATIVE);","-    expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished bad()\\n\");","+    assert_same(&op);","+    let expected = driver_transcript(&good_rejected(), ERR_NEGATIVE);","     for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","-        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &op));","-        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);","+        assert_eq!(output(lib, &op), expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);","     }"," }"," "]},{"oldStart":260,"oldLines":18,"newStart":284,"newLines":10,"lines":[" fn err_18_driver_only_good_rejects() {","     for (g, b) in [(10i32, 4i32), (-3, 0), (i32::MAX, 9), (i32::MIN, 5)] {","         let op = Op::Driver(g, b);","-        assert_same_forked(&op);","-        let mut expected = Vec::new();","-        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling good()...\\n\");","-        expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(7)));","-        expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_OOB);","-        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished good()\\n\");","-        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling bad()...\\n\");","-        expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(b as usize)));","-        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished bad()\\n\");","+        assert_same(&op);","+        let expected = driver_transcript(&good_rejected(), &ten_lines(Some(b as usize)));","         for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","-            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &op));","-            assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib driver({g},{b})\", lib.name);","+            assert_eq!(output(lib, &op), expected, \"{} lib driver({g},{b})\", lib.name);","         }","     }"," }"]},{"oldStart":281,"oldLines":18,"newStart":297,"newLines":12,"lines":[" fn err_19_driver_only_bad_rejects() {","     for (g, b) in [(0i32, -1i32), (7, i32::MIN), (9, -12345)] {","         let op = Op::Driver(g, b);","-        assert_same_forked(&op);","-        let mut expected = Vec::new();","-        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling good()...\\n\");","-        expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(7)));","-        expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(g as usize)));","-        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished good()\\n\");","-        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling bad()...\\n\");","-        expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_NEGATIVE);","-        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished bad()\\n\");","+        assert_same(&op);","+        let mut good_block = g2b_block();","+        good_block.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(g as usize)));","+        let expected = driver_transcript(&good_block, ERR_NEGATIVE);","         for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","-            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &op));","-            assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib driver({g},{b})\", lib.name);","+            assert_eq!(output(lib, &op), expected, \"{} lib driver({g},{b})\", lib.name);","         }","     }"," }"]},{"oldStart":300,"oldLines":22,"newStart":310,"newLines":30,"lines":[" /// ERRORS row 20 — extreme ints for both parameters across the FFI boundary."," #[test]"," fn err_20_driver_int_min_both() {","-    for (g, b) in [","+    let ops: Vec<Op> = [","         (i32::MIN, i32::MIN),","         (i32::MIN + 1, i32::MIN + 1),","         (i32::MAX, i32::MIN),","-    ] {","-        assert_same_forked(&Op::Driver(g, b));","+    ]","+    .iter()","+    .map(|&(g, b)| Op::Driver(g, b))","+    .collect();","+    assert_same_batch(&ops);","+    let expected = driver_transcript(&good_rejected(), ERR_NEGATIVE);","+    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","+        for (out, op) in outputs(lib, &ops).iter().zip(&ops) {","+            assert_eq!(out, &expected, \"{} lib {}\", lib.name, op.describe());","+        }","     }"," }"," "," /// ERRORS row 21 — non-NULL pointer to an immediate NUL: prints just \"\\n\"."," #[test]"," fn err_21_print_line_empty() {","-    assert_same_forked(&Op::PrintLine(vec![]));","+    let op = Op::PrintLine(vec![]);","+    assert_same(&op);","     for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","-        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::PrintLine(vec![])));","-        assert_eq!(out, b\"\\n\", \"{} lib\", lib.name);","+        assert_eq!(output(lib, &op), b\"\\n\", \"{} lib\", lib.name);","     }"," }"," "]},{"oldStart":323,"oldLines":52,"newStart":341,"newLines":57,"lines":[" #[test]"," fn err_22_print_line_embedded_nul() {","     let buf = b\"abc\\0def\\0\".to_vec();","-    for (off, want) in [","-        (0usize, &b\"abc\\n\"[..]),","+    let cases: [(usize, &[u8]); 5] = [","+        (0, b\"abc\\n\"),","         (1, b\"bc\\n\"),","         (3, b\"\\n\"),","         (4, b\"def\\n\"),","         (7, b\"\\n\"),","-    ] {","-        let op = Op::PrintLineRaw(buf.clone(), off);","-        assert_same(&op);","-        for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","-            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &op));","-            assert_eq!(out, want, \"{} lib {}\", lib.name, op.describe());","+    ];","+    let ops: Vec<Op> = cases","+        .iter()","+        .map(|&(off, _)| Op::PrintLineRaw(buf.clone(), off))","+        .collect();","+    assert_same_batch(&ops);","+    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","+        for (out, (off, want)) in outputs(lib, &ops).iter().zip(cases) {","+            assert_eq!(out, want, \"{} lib printLine(buf+{off})\", lib.name);","         }","     }"," }"," ","-/// ERRORS row 23 — format-specifier-looking payload is data, not a format.","+/// ERRORS row 23 — a format-specifier-looking payload is data, not a format."," #[test]"," fn err_23_print_line_format_like_data() {","-    for s in [&b\"%s\"[..], b\"%n\", b\"%d %d %d\", b\"%%%%\", b\"%1000000000d\", b\"%hn%p\"] {","-        let op = Op::PrintLine(s.to_vec());","-        assert_same_forked(&op);","-        let mut want = s.to_vec();","-        want.push(b'\\n');","-        for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","-            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &op));","-            assert_eq!(out, want, \"{} lib {}\", lib.name, op.describe());","+    let strings: [&[u8]; 6] = [b\"%s\", b\"%n\", b\"%d %d %d\", b\"%%%%\", b\"%1000000000d\", b\"%hn%p\"];","+    let ops: Vec<Op> = strings.iter().map(|s| Op::PrintLine(s.to_vec())).collect();","+    assert_same_batch(&ops);","+    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","+        for (out, s) in outputs(lib, &ops).iter().zip(strings) {","+            let mut want = s.to_vec();","+            want.push(b'\\n');","+            assert_eq!(out, &want, \"{} lib printLine({:?})\", lib.name, s);","         }","     }"," }"," "," /// ERRORS row 24 — extreme / \"out-of-range\" integer inputs.  This API has no","-/// enums, so the invalid-enum-variant class degenerates to arbitrary `int`s;","+/// enums, so the invalid-enum-variant class degenerates to arbitrary `int`s:"," /// they are all valid `%d` inputs and must format identically."," #[test]"," fn err_24_print_int_line_extremes() {","-    for n in [0, -1, 1, i32::MIN, i32::MIN + 1, i32::MAX, i32::MAX - 1] {","-        assert_same_forked(&Op::PrintIntLine(n));","-        let want = format!(\"{n}\\n\").into_bytes();","-        for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","-            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::PrintIntLine(n)));","-            assert_eq!(out, want, \"{} lib printIntLine({n})\", lib.name);","+    let values = [0, -1, 1, i32::MIN, i32::MIN + 1, i32::MAX, i32::MAX - 1];","+    let ops: Vec<Op> = values.iter().map(|&n| Op::PrintIntLine(n)).collect();","+    assert_same_batch(&ops);","+    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {","+        for (out, n) in outputs(lib, &ops).iter().zip(values) {","+            assert_eq!(out, &format!(\"{n}\\n\").into_bytes(), \"{} lib\", lib.name);","         }","     }","-    // values that are only representable as `unsigned` when reinterpreted","-    for u in [0x8000_0000u32, 0xFFFF_FFFF, 0x7FFF_FFFF, 0xDEAD_BEEF] {","-        assert_same(&Op::PrintIntLine(u as i32));","-    }","+    // bit patterns that are only \"positive\" when reinterpreted as unsigned","+    let ops2: Vec<Op> = [0x8000_0000u32, 0xFFFF_FFFF, 0x7FFF_FFFF, 0xDEAD_BEEF]","+        .iter()","+        .map(|&u| Op::PrintIntLine(u as i32))","+        .collect();","+    assert_same_batch(&ops2);"," }"]}],"originalFile":"//! Phase C — error-path differential tests.\n//!\n//! One test per row of `ERRORS.md`.  Every function in this C library is `void`\n//! and there is no `errno`/error-code/enum, so \"the same error/rejection\" means\n//! \"the same rejection message bytes on stdout and nothing else\", which is what\n//! each test asserts — against the C `.so`, against the Rust `.so`, and against\n//! the message text taken verbatim from `c_src/src/driver.c`.\n\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\n\n/// ERRORS row 1 — `printLine(NULL)`: `if(line != NULL)` fails ⇒ nothing at all.\n#[test]\nfn err_01_print_line_null() {\n    assert_same_forked(&Op::PrintLineNull);\n    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::PrintLineNull));\n        assert!(\n            out.is_empty(),\n            \"{} lib printed {:?} for printLine(NULL)\",\n            lib.name,\n            String::from_utf8_lossy(&out)\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 2 — `bad(-1)` ⇒ \"ERROR: Array index is negative.\".\n#[test]\nfn err_02_bad_negative_one() {\n    assert_same_forked(&Op::Bad(-1));\n    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Bad(-1)));\n        assert_eq!(out, ERR_NEGATIVE, \"{} lib\", lib.name);\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 3 — `bad(INT_MIN)`.\n#[test]\nfn err_03_bad_int_min() {\n    assert_same_forked(&Op::Bad(i32::MIN));\n    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Bad(i32::MIN)));\n        assert_eq!(out, ERR_NEGATIVE, \"{} lib\", lib.name);\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 4 — randomised negative `data`, 200 values.\n#[test]\nfn err_04_bad_negative_random() {\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0xE770_0004);\n    let mut values = vec![-1, -2, -10, i32::MIN, i32::MIN + 1, -1000000];\n    for _ in 0..200 {\n        values.push(rng.range_i32(i32::MIN, -1));\n    }\n    for d in values {\n        assert_same(&Op::Bad(d));\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(rust_lib(), &Op::Bad(d)));\n        assert_eq!(out, ERR_NEGATIVE, \"bad({d})\");\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 5 — `data >= 10` is *not* rejected (the injected flaw): the store\n/// is out of bounds, yet the ten in-bounds elements are still printed unchanged.\n#[test]\nfn err_05_bad_oob_not_rejected() {\n    for d in [10, 11, 13, 16, 20, 33, 64, 1000] {\n        let (c, r) = diff_forked(&Op::Bad(d));\n        assert_eq!(\n            c.stdout,\n            ten_lines(None),\n            \"C lib: bad({d}) should print ten zeros (OOB store misses the array)\"\n        );\n        assert_eq!(\n            r.stdout, c.stdout,\n            \"Rust lib diverged from C for bad({d})\"\n        );\n        assert!(\n            !c.stdout.starts_with(ERR_NEGATIVE),\n            \"C lib must NOT reject bad({d})\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 6 — `bad(10)`, the very first out-of-range index.\n#[test]\nfn err_06_bad_oob_first() {\n    assert_same_stdout_forked(&Op::Bad(10));\n    let (c, _) = diff_forked(&Op::Bad(10));\n    assert_eq!(c.stdout, ten_lines(None));\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 7 — `bad(INT_MAX)`: accepted by `data >= 0`, store far off-stack.\n#[test]\nfn err_07_bad_int_max() {\n    assert_same_stdout_forked(&Op::Bad(i32::MAX));\n    assert_same_stdout_forked(&Op::Bad(i32::MAX - 1));\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 8 — `good(-1)` ⇒ goodG2B block + \"out-of-bounds\" message.\n#[test]\nfn err_08_good_negative() {\n    assert_same_forked(&Op::Good(-1));\n    let mut expected = ten_lines(Some(7));\n    expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_OOB);\n    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Good(-1)));\n        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 9 — `good(INT_MIN)`.\n#[test]\nfn err_09_good_int_min() {\n    assert_same_forked(&Op::Good(i32::MIN));\n    let mut expected = ten_lines(Some(7));\n    expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_OOB);\n    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Good(i32::MIN)));\n        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 10 — `good(10)`: first value failing `data < (10)`.\n#[test]\nfn err_10_good_ten() {\n    assert_same_forked(&Op::Good(10));\n    let mut expected = ten_lines(Some(7));\n    expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_OOB);\n    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Good(10)));\n        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);\n    }\n    // one step inside the range is accepted, one step outside is rejected\n    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n        let inside = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Good(9)));\n        assert!(!inside.ends_with(ERR_OOB), \"{} lib rejected good(9)\", lib.name);\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 11 — `good(INT_MAX)`.\n#[test]\nfn err_11_good_int_max() {\n    assert_same_forked(&Op::Good(i32::MAX));\n    let mut expected = ten_lines(Some(7));\n    expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_OOB);\n    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Good(i32::MAX)));\n        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 12 — randomised out-of-range `data` for `goodB2G`, 200 values.\n#[test]\nfn err_12_good_out_of_range_random() {\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0xE770_0012);\n    let mut expected = ten_lines(Some(7));\n    expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_OOB);\n    for i in 0..200 {\n        let d = if i % 2 == 0 {\n            rng.range_i32(i32::MIN, -1)\n        } else {\n            rng.range_i32(10, i32::MAX)\n        };\n        assert_same(&Op::Good(d));\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(rust_lib(), &Op::Good(d)));\n        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"good({d})\");\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 13 — `good(9)` is the last accepted value.\n#[test]\nfn err_13_good_nine_accepted() {\n    assert_same_forked(&Op::Good(9));\n    let mut expected = ten_lines(Some(7));\n    expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(9)));\n    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Good(9)));\n        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 14 — `good(0)` is the lower boundary and is accepted.\n#[test]\nfn err_14_good_zero_accepted() {\n    assert_same_forked(&Op::Good(0));\n    let mut expected = ten_lines(Some(7));\n    expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(0)));\n    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Good(0)));\n        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 15 — `bad(0)` / `bad(9)`: the boundaries the missing upper-bound\n/// check would have used are accepted and in bounds.\n#[test]\nfn err_15_bad_boundaries_accepted() {\n    for (d, idx) in [(0i32, 0usize), (9, 9)] {\n        assert_same_forked(&Op::Bad(d));\n        for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Bad(d)));\n            assert_eq!(out, ten_lines(Some(idx)), \"{} lib bad({d})\", lib.name);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 16 — `goodG2B`'s \"negative\" branch is unreachable (`data` == 7), so\n/// neither library may ever print that message from `good`/`driver`.\n#[test]\nfn err_16_goodg2b_error_branch_unreachable() {\n    let mut rng = Rng::new(0xE770_0016);\n    let mut values = vec![-1, 0, 7, 9, 10, i32::MIN, i32::MAX];\n    for _ in 0..100 {\n        values.push(rng.next_i32());\n    }\n    for d in values {\n        for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::Good(d)));\n            assert!(\n                !contains(&out, ERR_NEGATIVE),\n                \"{} lib printed the goodG2B 'negative' message for good({d})\",\n                lib.name\n            );\n            // the goodG2B block (index 7 set) always comes first\n            assert!(\n                out.starts_with(&ten_lines(Some(7))),\n                \"{} lib: good({d}) did not start with goodG2B's fixed block\",\n                lib.name\n            );\n        }\n        assert_same(&Op::Good(d));\n    }\n}\n\nfn contains(hay: &[u8], needle: &[u8]) -> bool {\n    hay.windows(needle.len()).any(|w| w == needle)\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 17 — `driver` with both error branches taken at once.\n#[test]\nfn err_17_driver_both_error_branches() {\n    let op = Op::Driver(-5, -9);\n    assert_same_forked(&op);\n    let mut expected = Vec::new();\n    expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling good()...\\n\");\n    expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(7)));\n    expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_OOB);\n    expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished good()\\n\");\n    expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling bad()...\\n\");\n    expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_NEGATIVE);\n    expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished bad()\\n\");\n    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &op));\n        assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib\", lib.name);\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 18 — only `good`'s check rejects.\n#[test]\nfn err_18_driver_only_good_rejects() {\n    for (g, b) in [(10i32, 4i32), (-3, 0), (i32::MAX, 9), (i32::MIN, 5)] {\n        let op = Op::Driver(g, b);\n        assert_same_forked(&op);\n        let mut expected = Vec::new();\n        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling good()...\\n\");\n        expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(7)));\n        expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_OOB);\n        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished good()\\n\");\n        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling bad()...\\n\");\n        expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(b as usize)));\n        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished bad()\\n\");\n        for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &op));\n            assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib driver({g},{b})\", lib.name);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 19 — only `bad`'s check rejects.\n#[test]\nfn err_19_driver_only_bad_rejects() {\n    for (g, b) in [(0i32, -1i32), (7, i32::MIN), (9, -12345)] {\n        let op = Op::Driver(g, b);\n        assert_same_forked(&op);\n        let mut expected = Vec::new();\n        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling good()...\\n\");\n        expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(7)));\n        expected.extend_from_slice(&ten_lines(Some(g as usize)));\n        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished good()\\n\");\n        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Calling bad()...\\n\");\n        expected.extend_from_slice(ERR_NEGATIVE);\n        expected.extend_from_slice(b\"Finished bad()\\n\");\n        for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &op));\n            assert_eq!(out, expected, \"{} lib driver({g},{b})\", lib.name);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 20 — extreme ints for both parameters across the FFI boundary.\n#[test]\nfn err_20_driver_int_min_both() {\n    for (g, b) in [\n        (i32::MIN, i32::MIN),\n        (i32::MIN + 1, i32::MIN + 1),\n        (i32::MAX, i32::MIN),\n    ] {\n        assert_same_forked(&Op::Driver(g, b));\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 21 — non-NULL pointer to an immediate NUL: prints just \"\\n\".\n#[test]\nfn err_21_print_line_empty() {\n    assert_same_forked(&Op::PrintLine(vec![]));\n    for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n        let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::PrintLine(vec![])));\n        assert_eq!(out, b\"\\n\", \"{} lib\", lib.name);\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 22 — interior pointer / embedded NUL truncation.\n#[test]\nfn err_22_print_line_embedded_nul() {\n    let buf = b\"abc\\0def\\0\".to_vec();\n    for (off, want) in [\n        (0usize, &b\"abc\\n\"[..]),\n        (1, b\"bc\\n\"),\n        (3, b\"\\n\"),\n        (4, b\"def\\n\"),\n        (7, b\"\\n\"),\n    ] {\n        let op = Op::PrintLineRaw(buf.clone(), off);\n        assert_same(&op);\n        for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &op));\n            assert_eq!(out, want, \"{} lib {}\", lib.name, op.describe());\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 23 — format-specifier-looking payload is data, not a format.\n#[test]\nfn err_23_print_line_format_like_data() {\n    for s in [&b\"%s\"[..], b\"%n\", b\"%d %d %d\", b\"%%%%\", b\"%1000000000d\", b\"%hn%p\"] {\n        let op = Op::PrintLine(s.to_vec());\n        assert_same_forked(&op);\n        let mut want = s.to_vec();\n        want.push(b'\\n');\n        for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &op));\n            assert_eq!(out, want, \"{} lib {}\", lib.name, op.describe());\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// ERRORS row 24 — extreme / \"out-of-range\" integer inputs.  This API has no\n/// enums, so the invalid-enum-variant class degenerates to arbitrary `int`s;\n/// they are all valid `%d` inputs and must format identically.\n#[test]\nfn err_24_print_int_line_extremes() {\n    for n in [0, -1, 1, i32::MIN, i32::MIN + 1, i32::MAX, i32::MAX - 1] {\n        assert_same_forked(&Op::PrintIntLine(n));\n        let want = format!(\"{n}\\n\").into_bytes();\n        for lib in [c_lib(), rust_lib()] {\n            let out = capture_inproc(|| run_op(lib, &Op::PrintIntLine(n)));\n            assert_eq!(out, want, \"{} lib printIntLine({n})\", lib.name);\n        }\n    }\n    // values that are only representable as `unsigned` when reinterpreted\n    for u in [0x8000_0000u32, 0xFFFF_FFFF, 0x7FFF_FFFF, 0xDEAD_BEEF] {\n        assert_same(&Op::PrintIntLine(u as i32));\n    }\n}\n","userModified":false}}
