{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_h7pmwkp6lrvmyvkhn56niubiz3hfa7r5j3x5jiju645rbdzi5zra","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass across every configuration.\n\n## What was verified\n\n**Phase A — surface map** (three artifacts in `translated_rust/`, all derived mechanically from the C):\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — all 5 dynamic symbols from `nm -D` on the C `.so` (`printLine`, `printIntLine`, `bad`, `good`, `driver`); **0 missing** from the Rust `.so`. The 2 `static` C functions (`goodG2B`, `goodB2G`) correctly stay unexported on both sides. No C source was left untranslated — `driver.c` is the whole library.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 24 rows, from grepping every `if`/`NULL`/`ERROR`/constant in the C (there are no asserts, no return codes, no errno, no enums — every function is `void`, so rejection is observable only through stdout).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 29 rows: all 5 entry points including the low-level printers, × input shapes (NULL, byte values 1–255, 65 KB payloads, format-specifier data, embedded NULs, interior pointers, `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`, exhaustive index sweeps), × sequencing/buffering/statelessness/composition axes.\n\n**Phases B & C** — `tests/valid_paths.rs` (28 tests) and `tests/error_paths.rs` (24 tests) load **both** `.so`s via `libloading` (`RTLD_NOW|RTLD_LOCAL`) and call only `dlsym`-resolved symbols, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are what's tested. Output is captured at the fd level inside `fork()`ed children (libtest's own fd-1 writes made in-process redirection unsafe), with per-call offsets so a single fork yields each call's exact bytes. ~6 000 differential calls per profile, fixed-seed randomized.\n\n**Phase D** — `tests/symbols.rs` re-derives the `nm -D` diff on every run (reaches empty), and `run_all_configs.sh` enumerates feature combinations (`Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`, `src/` no `#[cfg(feature)]`, CMake no options ⇒ exactly one combination) × both cargo profiles: **24 + 28 + 3 tests pass in `dev` and in `release`**.\n\n## Findings\n\nNo divergence exists in the well-defined input domain — `src/lib.rs` needed no changes; it is byte-identical to the C for every `printLine`/`printIntLine` input, `bad(data ≤ 9)`, `good(any int)`, and `driver(*, badData ≤ 9)`.\n\nThe one deliberate exception is documented in `ERRORS.md`/`VERIFICATION.md`: `bad(data)` checks only `data >= 0` (the injected CWE-129 flaw, faithfully preserved), so `data >= 10` stores 4 bytes past the array. There the C specifies only \"write at `&buffer[0] + 4*data` on the stack\"; whether that lands on padding, a saved register or a return address is a compiler frame-layout property. Those rows therefore require identical streams when both processes survive and prefix-equality when the smash kills one. Measured: stdout identical for every OOB value in `dev`; in `release` only `driver(_, 12..13)` differs (gcc's saved `rbp` vs the optimized Rust `driver`'s return address). I evaluated a padding hack in Rust's `bad` and rejected it — it trades those 2 mismatches for 3 others, so the unpadded, faithful translation is the closest match."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":923,"cache_read_input_tokens":172836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":923,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0af81b2f-19bc-46ab-9c71-7e73412f8759","uuid":"d893d9ef-4006-4459-8949-eb4645541781","timestamp":"2026-08-18T00:44:48.837Z"}
